{"siren:The chair described the consultation as “a clear mandate to proceed”. The report itself was more circumspect: most respondents supported the aim, while several questioned whether the proposed safeguards could be enforced. An adviser argued that delaying action would itself distribute risks, chiefly to people absent from the consultation. A critic replied that urgency might justify a provisional measure, but could not retrospectively turn an uneven consultation into informed consent. Both accepted that doing nothing had costs; they disagreed about what that fact authorised.":"f2e446574cdec79087ce05fca2187c16ef52d62b2f792284eba791e46ad37039","lauren:I'm going to call the police for help.":"c123a97e8579ecda0241b15e6ce528835e2589f2091020afac80c4afff857ba5"}